Rast wrote:
> Don wrote on Thu, 09 Dec 2004 18:25:23 GMT:
>>If pudding farming is abusive, then make puddings not split.
> 
> 
> The original purpose of the pudding split was to make them challenging 
> in an interesting way.  You're fighting a pudding, you hit it twice, 
> and ohnoes! now there are three puddings attacking you.  Of course, now 
> it is being abused to create infinite puddings and obtain infinite 
> death drops, sacrifices, food, intrinsics...

Right, but the thing is its a character-buffness-range thing.
Some characters can't take a single pudding.
Some can kill them like hot cakes.
There is a range inbetween that could take one but not 3.
These are the guys who would say "Oh No!  3 puddings!".
The first case would run away with 1, the second case would say
"Yay! More puddings!  Wheres my altar?"

So, while I understand the original purpose of the pudding split,
I think its not a terribly important feature of the game, doesn't
achieve its purpose ("Oh no!") very often, so if it causes an
abuse problem, give it the axe.

> My solution would be to limit each pudding to splitting 3 times.  So a 
> single wild pudding could be "farmed" into eight puddings, but no more 
> puddings could be created from those 8.
> 
> IIRC, currently when a pudding splits each half has 50% of the HP.  I 
> suggest that each half should have 70% of the HP.

I totally agree with you here.  This is a better solution to
"no split" as long as its not too much of a hassle to implement.
If it is a hassle then I think the "no split" option should still
be considered.  The idea of basing the splits on HP may actually make
it pretty easy to implement and in that case, I think its a great idea.
(Newton's 4th law : "Conservation of pudding mass" and all that.)

Cool... someone who sort of agrees with me on r.g.r.n!
How refreshing! :)

